/*  Patterns — `RegexPattern.Compile` in `src/Interpreter/RegexPattern.cs`, which the C# parser
    calls on the text of `Define regex <name> as [ … ]` and lowers to an ordinary function.

    The pattern is read into a small tree of its own (a `node`, reused: `Ch`, `Any`, `Cat`, `Or`,
    `Star`, `Plus`, `Opt`, the anchors, `NoneOf`), then built into the automaton the engine in
    `Prelude/regex.cufe` runs: a series of states, each a kind, a text and two successors.

    ⚠ FINDING: Cufet cannot ask a character for its code point, and `[a-z]` is a range of them. A
    chase goes the other way — a number inserted into one IS a character — so a table from
    character to number is built from that, once, and only when a pattern has a range in it.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    Define object pattern-reader with (
        the chase source,
        the number size,
        the number at,
        the fact folding,
        the fact dot-all,
        the fact multiline,
        the map from text to number codes,
        the number declared-row,
        the number declared-column).

    // ── Where the reader stands ───────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind text to char-at unto pattern-reader, given (the number spot):
        If spot is greater than one's size, return "".
        Return item spot of one's source.
    Done.

    Bind text to peek-char unto pattern-reader:
        Return cast one's char-at on (one's at).
    Done.

    Bind fact to at-end unto pattern-reader:
        Return one's at is greater than one's size.
    Done.

    /// The fault, in the voice the C# parser gives it: what, why, and the fix with a capital.
    Bind text to fault unto pattern-reader, given (the text what, the text why, the text fix):
        Define lead as the first 1 characters of fix.
        Define rest as the characters from 2 to the end of fix.
        Return "error\t{one's declared-row}\t{one's declared-column}\t{what} — {why}. {lead in uppercase}{rest}.".
    Done.

    // ── Code points ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// A character's code point, from a table built the first time one is asked for.
    Bind number to code-of unto pattern-reader, given (the text ch):
        If the size of one's codes is 0:
            Define every as a chase.
            Define point as 0.
            While point is less than 12288, repeat:
                If point is less than 55296 or point is greater than 57343, insert point into every.
                Increment point by 1.
            Done.
            Define place as 0.
            For each held in every, repeat:
                In one's codes, the entry for held becomes place.
                Increment place by 1.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return (the entry for ch in one's codes) but void is -1.
    Done.

    Bind text to char-of, given (the number point):
        Define one-char as a chase.
        Insert point into one-char.
        Return one-char converted to text.
    Done.

    // ── Case ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// Both cases of every character, when `(?i)` is in force.
    Bind text to folded unto pattern-reader, given (the text members):
        If one's folding is false, return members.
        Define both as a chase.
        Define each-char as a chase.
        Insert members into each-char.
        For each ch in each-char, repeat:
            Insert ch into both.
            Define upper as ch in uppercase.
            Define lower as ch in lowercase.
            If the length of upper is 1 and upper is not ch, insert upper into both.
            If the length of lower is 1 and lower is not ch, insert lower into both.
        Done.
        Return both converted to text.
    Done.

    // ── The pattern's own tree ────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind node to leaf-node, given (the text kind, the text value):
        Return a new node { the kind kind, the word value, the children a series of node }.
    Done.

    Bind node to pair-node, given (the text kind, the node left, the node right):
        Return cast made on (kind, a series with (left, right)).
    Done.

    Bind node to wrap-node, given (the text kind, the node inner):
        Return cast made on (kind, a series with (inner)).
    Done.

    /// An alternation over every character of `members`.
    Bind node to admitting, given (the text members):
        Define each-char as a chase.
        Insert members into each-char.
        Define built as cast nothing.
        Define started as false.
        For each ch in each-char, repeat:
            If started:
                The built becomes cast pair-node on ("Or", built, cast leaf-node on ("Ch", ch)).
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                The built becomes cast leaf-node on ("Ch", ch).
                The started becomes true.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return built.
    Done.

    Bind node to character unto pattern-reader, given (the text ch):
        If one's folding, return cast admitting on (cast one's folded on (ch)).
        Return cast leaf-node on ("Ch", ch).
    Done.

    Bind text to shorthand-members, given (the text letter):
        If letter is "d", return "0123456789".
        If letter is "w", return "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789_".
        If letter is "s":
            Define spaces as a chase.
            Insert " \t\n\r" into spaces.
            Insert 12 into spaces.
            Insert 11 into spaces.
            Return spaces converted to text.
        Done.
        Return "".
    Done.

    Bind fact to is-negated-shorthand, given (the text letter):
        If cast shorthand-members on (letter in lowercase) is "", return false.
        Return letter is not (letter in lowercase).
    Done.

    Bind fact to is-meta, given (the text ch):
        If ch is "", return false.
        Return "*+?|().[]^$\{\}" contains ch.
    Done.

    Bind text to typed-directly, given (the text letter):
        If letter is "t", return "a tab".
        If letter is "n", return "a line break".
        If letter is "r", return "a carriage return".
        Return "".
    Done.

    // ── Reading ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind node or failure to read-alternation unto pattern-reader:
        Define left as cast one's read-sequence or pass the failure off.
        While cast one's at-end is false and cast one's peek-char is "|", repeat:
            Increment one's at by 1.
            Define right as cast one's read-sequence or pass the failure off.
            The left becomes cast pair-node on ("Or", left, right).
        Done.
        Return left.
    Done.

    Bind fact to is-ascii-letter, given (the text ch):
        If ch is "", return false.
        Return "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ" contains ch.
    Done.

    /// `(?i)`, `(?s:`, `(?is)` … — applies the letters and answers whether the group is scoped.
    /// Answers "none" and leaves the reader alone for anything else.
    Bind text or failure to take-flags unto pattern-reader:
        If cast one's at-end or cast one's peek-char is not "(" or cast one's char-at on (one's at + 1) is not "?":
            Return "none".
        Done.
        Define scan as one's at + 2.
        While cast is-ascii-letter on (cast one's char-at on (scan)), repeat:
            Increment scan by 1.
        Done.
        If scan is one's at + 2, return "none".
        Define terminator as cast one's char-at on (scan).
        If terminator is not ")" and terminator is not ":", return "none".
        Define spot as one's at + 2.
        While spot is less than scan, repeat:
            Define flag-letter as cast one's char-at on (spot).
            If flag-letter is "i":
                One's folding becomes true.
            Done.
            Otherwise if flag-letter is "s":
                One's dot-all becomes true.
            Done.
            Otherwise if flag-letter is "m":
                One's multiline becomes true.
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Return a failure (cast one's fault on ("'{flag-letter}' is not a flag this pattern understands",
                    "the flags are 'i' to ignore case, 's' to let '.' cross a line break, and 'm' to make '^' and '$' mean each line",
                    "write '(?i)', '(?s)', '(?m)' or any of them together")).
            Done.
            Increment spot by 1.
        Done.
        One's at becomes scan + 1.
        Return "scoped" when terminator is ":", otherwise "bare".
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to read-sequence unto pattern-reader:
        Define built as cast nothing.
        Define started as false.
        Define scanning as true.
        While scanning, repeat:
            If cast one's at-end, stop.
            Define here as cast one's peek-char.
            If here is "|" or here is ")", stop.
            Define before as one's at.
            Define was-folding as one's folding.
            Define was-dot-all as one's dot-all.
            Define was-multiline as one's multiline.
            Define flags as cast one's take-flags or pass the failure off.
            If flags is "bare", skip.
            If flags is "scoped":
                One's at becomes before.
                One's folding becomes was-folding.
                One's dot-all becomes was-dot-all.
                One's multiline becomes was-multiline.
            Done.
            Define piece as cast one's read-repeated or pass the failure off.
            If started:
                The built becomes cast pair-node on ("Cat", built, piece).
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                The built becomes piece.
                The started becomes true.
            Done.
        Done.
        If started is false:
            Return a failure (cast one's fault on ("this pattern has an empty alternative",
                "one side of a '|' has nothing on it, which would match everywhere",
                "write what that side should find, or drop the '|'")).
        Done.
        Return built.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to read-repeated unto pattern-reader:
        Define inner as cast one's read-atom or pass the failure off.
        Define scanning as true.
        While scanning, repeat:
            If cast one's at-end, stop.
            Define mark as cast one's peek-char.
            If mark is "\{":
                The inner becomes cast one's read-count on (inner) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Otherwise if mark is "*" or mark is "+" or mark is "?":
                Increment one's at by 1.
                Define shape as "Star" when mark is "*", otherwise ("Plus" when mark is "+", otherwise "Opt").
                The inner becomes cast wrap-node on (shape, inner).
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Stop.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return inner.
    Done.

    /// Digits, or -1 when there are none.
    Bind number to read-count-number unto pattern-reader:
        Define digits as "".
        While cast one's at-end is false and "0123456789" contains cast one's peek-char, repeat:
            The digits becomes digits joined to cast one's peek-char.
            Increment one's at by 1.
        Done.
        If digits is "", return -1.
        If the length of digits is greater than 6, return 1001.
        Return (digits converted to number) but void is 1001.
    Done.

    /// `{n}`, `{n,}` or `{n,m}` — desugared to repetition of what came before it.
    Bind node or failure to read-count unto pattern-reader, given (the node inner):
        Increment one's at by 1.
        Define least as cast one's read-count-number.
        Define most as least.
        Define open-ended as false.
        If cast one's at-end is false and cast one's peek-char is ",":
            Increment one's at by 1.
            If cast one's at-end is false and cast one's peek-char is "\}":
                The open-ended becomes true.
                The most becomes -1.
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                The most becomes cast one's read-count-number.
            Done.
        Done.
        If cast one's at-end or cast one's peek-char is not "\}":
            Return a failure (cast one's fault on ("this count is never closed",
                "a count is written '\{n\}', '\{n,\}' or '\{n,m\}'", "write '\\\{' if you meant the character")).
        Done.
        Increment one's at by 1.
        If least is -1 or (open-ended is false and most is -1):
            Return a failure (cast one's fault on ("this count has no number in it",
                "a count says how many times to repeat, so it needs a number",
                "write '\{2\}', '\{2,\}' or '\{2,5\}' — or '\\\{' for the character")).
        Done.
        If open-ended is false and most is less than least:
            Return a failure (cast one's fault on ("'\{{least},{most}\}' counts down, from {least} to {most}",
                "a count goes from the smaller number to the larger one", "write '\{{most},{least}\}'")).
        Done.
        If least is 0 and open-ended is false and most is 0:
            Return a failure (cast one's fault on ("'\{0\}' repeats nothing zero times",
                "a count of zero leaves nothing behind, so the pattern could never use it",
                "remove it, or write '\{0,1\}' for something optional")).
        Done.
        If least is greater than 1000 or most is greater than 1000:
            Return a failure (cast one's fault on ("a count above 1000 is more than this pattern will build",
                "a count is written out as that many copies, so a large one becomes a very large automaton",
                "use a repeat like '+' or '*' instead of counting past 1000")).
        Done.
        Return cast repeated on (inner, least, most).
    Done.

    /// `least` copies, then a star (when `most` is -1) or nested options up to `most`.
    Bind node to repeated, given (the node inner, the number least, the number most):
        Define built as cast nothing.
        Define started as false.
        If most is -1:
            The built becomes cast wrap-node on ("Star", inner).
            The started becomes true.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            Define count as 0.
            While count is less than most - least, repeat:
                If started:
                    The built becomes cast wrap-node on ("Opt", cast pair-node on ("Cat", inner, built)).
                Done.
                Otherwise:
                    The built becomes cast wrap-node on ("Opt", inner).
                    The started becomes true.
                Done.
                Increment count by 1.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define count as 0.
        While count is less than least, repeat:
            If started:
                The built becomes cast pair-node on ("Cat", inner, built).
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                The built becomes inner.
                The started becomes true.
            Done.
            Increment count by 1.
        Done.
        Return built.
    Done.

    Bind text to group-extension unto pattern-reader:
        Define next-char as cast one's char-at on (one's at + 1).
        If next-char is "=" or next-char is "!":
            Return cast one's fault on ("this pattern uses lookahead, which an automaton cannot express",
                "lookahead asks what comes next without consuming it, which needs a machine that can backtrack — and backtracking is what lets a pattern hang forever, so this book does not have one",
                "match what you mean to consume, or split the question into two patterns").
        Done.
        Define after-next as cast one's char-at on (one's at + 2).
        If next-char is "<" and (after-next is "=" or after-next is "!"):
            Return cast one's fault on ("this pattern uses lookbehind, which an automaton cannot express",
                "lookbehind asks what came before without consuming it, which needs a machine that can backtrack — and backtracking is what lets a pattern hang forever, so this book does not have one",
                "match what you mean to consume, or split the question into two patterns").
        Done.
        If next-char is "<":
            Return cast one's fault on ("this pattern names a capture, which patterns cannot do yet",
                "a pattern answers whether the subject holds a match, and gives back no part of what it matched",
                "use the group without a name").
        Done.
        If next-char is "i" or next-char is "m" or next-char is "s" or next-char is "x":
            Return cast one's fault on ("'(?{next-char}' is not a flag this pattern understands",
                "the only flag is 'i' for ignoring case, written '(?i)' to the end of the group or '(?i:…)' around part of it",
                "write '(?i)' on its own, or '(?i:' around what it should cover").
        Done.
        Return cast one's fault on ("'(?{next-char}' is not something this pattern understands",
            "a '(' opens a group, and '(?:' opens one that captures nothing", "write '\\(' if you meant the character").
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to read-atom unto pattern-reader:
        If cast one's at-end:
            Return a failure (cast one's fault on ("this pattern is empty",
                "a pattern with nothing in it would match everywhere, which is never what was meant",
                "write the text the pattern should find")).
        Done.
        Define ch as cast one's peek-char.
        If ch is "*" or ch is "+" or ch is "?":
            Return a failure (cast one's fault on ("'{ch}' has nothing before it to repeat",
                "a repeat applies to whatever comes just before it", "write '\\{ch}' if you meant the character itself")).
        Done.
        If ch is "^":
            Increment one's at by 1.
            Return cast leaf-node on ("AtLineStart" when one's multiline, otherwise "AtStart", "").
        Done.
        If ch is "$":
            Increment one's at by 1.
            Return cast leaf-node on ("AtLineEnd" when one's multiline, otherwise "AtEnd", "").
        Done.
        If ch is "[":
            Increment one's at by 1.
            Return cast one's read-class or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If ch is "(":
            Increment one's at by 1.
            Define outer-folding as one's folding.
            Define outer-dot-all as one's dot-all.
            Define outer-multiline as one's multiline.
            If cast one's at-end is false and cast one's peek-char is "?" and cast one's char-at on (one's at + 1) is ":":
                Increment one's at by 2.
            Done.
            Otherwise if cast one's at-end is false and cast one's peek-char is "?":
                Decrement one's at by 1.
                Define flags as cast one's take-flags or pass the failure off.
                If flags is not "scoped":
                    Increment one's at by 1.
                    Return a failure (cast one's group-extension).
                Done.
            Done.
            Define inside as cast one's read-alternation or pass the failure off.
            If cast one's at-end or cast one's peek-char is not ")":
                Return a failure (cast one's fault on ("this pattern opens a group that is never closed",
                    "every '(' needs a ')' after it", "write '\\(' if you meant the character")).
            Done.
            Increment one's at by 1.
            One's folding becomes outer-folding.
            One's dot-all becomes outer-dot-all.
            One's multiline becomes outer-multiline.
            Return inside.
        Done.
        If ch is ".":
            Increment one's at by 1.
            If one's dot-all, return cast leaf-node on ("Any", "").
            Return cast leaf-node on ("NoneOf", "\n").
        Done.
        If ch is "\\":
            If one's at + 1 is greater than one's size:
                Return a failure (cast one's fault on ("this pattern ends in a backslash, which escapes nothing",
                    "a backslash makes the character after it ordinary, so there has to be one",
                    "write '\\\\' for a backslash you meant literally")).
            Done.
            Define escaped-char as cast one's char-at on (one's at + 1).
            Define members as cast shorthand-members on (escaped-char).
            If members is not "":
                Increment one's at by 2.
                Return cast admitting on (cast one's folded on (members)).
            Done.
            If cast is-negated-shorthand on (escaped-char):
                Increment one's at by 2.
                Return cast leaf-node on ("NoneOf", cast one's folded on (cast shorthand-members on (escaped-char in lowercase))).
            Done.
            If escaped-char is not "\\" and cast is-meta on (escaped-char) is false:
                Define spelled-as as cast typed-directly on (escaped-char).
                Define fix as "write '{escaped-char}' on its own if you meant the character".
                If spelled-as is not "", the fix becomes "write {spelled-as} straight into the pattern — it needs no escape".
                Return a failure (cast one's fault on ("'\\{escaped-char}' is not an escape this pattern understands",
                    "a backslash may make a metacharacter ordinary, or stand for a backslash", fix)).
            Done.
            Increment one's at by 2.
            Return cast one's character on (escaped-char).
        Done.
        Increment one's at by 1.
        Return cast one's character on (ch).
    Done.

    /// One character inside a class, with escapes honoured.
    Bind text or failure to class-character unto pattern-reader:
        Define ch as cast one's peek-char.
        If ch is not "\\":
            Increment one's at by 1.
            Return ch.
        Done.
        If one's at + 1 is greater than one's size:
            Return a failure (cast one's fault on ("this class ends in a backslash, which escapes nothing",
                "a backslash makes the character after it ordinary, so there has to be one",
                "write '\\\\' for a backslash you meant literally")).
        Done.
        Define escaped-char as cast one's char-at on (one's at + 1).
        If escaped-char is not "\\" and escaped-char is not "]" and escaped-char is not "[" and escaped-char is not "-" and escaped-char is not "^":
            Define spelled-as as cast typed-directly on (escaped-char).
            Define fix as "write '{escaped-char}' on its own if you meant the character".
            If spelled-as is not "", the fix becomes "write {spelled-as} straight into the class — it needs no escape".
            Return a failure (cast one's fault on ("'\\{escaped-char}' is not an escape a class understands",
                "inside a class a backslash may precede a backslash, a bracket, a dash, a caret, or one of the shorthands \\d \\w \\s", fix)).
        Done.
        Increment one's at by 2.
        Return escaped-char.
    Done.

    /// `[ … ]` — an alternation of what it admits, or one NoneOf state when negated.
    Bind node or failure to read-class unto pattern-reader:
        Define negated as cast one's at-end is false and cast one's peek-char is "^".
        If negated, increment one's at by 1.
        Define admitted as a chase.
        While cast one's at-end is false and cast one's peek-char is not "]", repeat:
            If cast one's peek-char is "\\" and one's at + 1 is not greater than one's size:
                Define letter as cast one's char-at on (one's at + 1).
                Define members as cast shorthand-members on (letter).
                If members is not "":
                    Increment one's at by 2.
                    Insert members into admitted.
                    Skip.
                Done.
                If cast is-negated-shorthand on (letter):
                    Return a failure (cast one's fault on ("'\\{letter}' cannot be used inside a class",
                        "a class is the characters it admits, and a negated shorthand is every character except some — the two cannot be listed together",
                        "write '\\{letter}' on its own, outside the brackets")).
                Done.
            Done.
            Define low as cast one's class-character or pass the failure off.
            If cast one's at-end is false and cast one's peek-char is "-" and cast one's char-at on (one's at + 1) is not "]" and one's at + 1 is not greater than one's size:
                Increment one's at by 1.
                Define high as cast one's class-character or pass the failure off.
                Define from-point as cast one's code-of on (low).
                Define to-point as cast one's code-of on (high).
                If from-point is -1 or to-point is -1:
                    Return a failure "unsupported\t{one's declared-row}\t{one's declared-column}\ta class range beyond the characters this parser can number".
                Done.
                If to-point is less than from-point:
                    Return a failure (cast one's fault on ("'{low}-{high}' is a range that runs backwards",
                        "a range goes from the earlier character to the later one", "write '{high}-{low}'")).
                Done.
                Define point as from-point.
                While point is not greater than to-point, repeat:
                    Insert point into admitted.
                    Increment point by 1.
                Done.
                Skip.
            Done.
            Insert low into admitted.
        Done.
        If cast one's at-end or cast one's peek-char is not "]":
            Return a failure (cast one's fault on ("this pattern opens a class that is never closed",
                "every '[' needs a ']' after it", "write '\\[' if you meant the character")).
        Done.
        Increment one's at by 1.
        If the number of admitted is 0:
            If negated:
                Return a failure (cast one's fault on ("this class excludes nothing",
                    "a negated class with no characters in it admits every character, which '.' already says",
                    "write '.' for any character, or list the characters to exclude")).
            Done.
            Return a failure (cast one's fault on ("this class is empty",
                "a class with no characters in it admits nothing, so the pattern could never match",
                "list the characters it should admit")).
        Done.
        Define chosen as cast one's folded on (admitted converted to text).
        If negated, return cast leaf-node on ("NoneOf", chosen).
        Return cast admitting on (chosen).
    Done.

    // ── Building the automaton ────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind number to emit-state, given (the series of records like (the number kind, the text ch, the number step, the number alt) states,
            the number kind, the text ch, the number step, the number alt):
        Insert a record with (the kind kind, the ch ch, the step step, the alt alt) into states.
        Return the number of states.
    Done.

    /// Compiles `tree` so that finishing it lands on `next`, and answers where it is entered.
    Bind number to build-state, given (the series of records like (the number kind, the text ch, the number step, the number alt) states,
            the node tree, the number next):
        Define kind as tree's kind.
        If kind is "Ch", return cast emit-state on (states, 0, tree's word, next, 0).
        If kind is "Any", return cast emit-state on (states, 1, "", next, 0).
        If kind is "AtStart", return cast emit-state on (states, 4, "", next, 0).
        If kind is "AtEnd", return cast emit-state on (states, 5, "", next, 0).
        If kind is "AtLineStart", return cast emit-state on (states, 7, "\n", next, 0).
        If kind is "AtLineEnd", return cast emit-state on (states, 8, "\n", next, 0).
        If kind is "NoneOf", return cast emit-state on (states, 6, tree's word, next, 0).
        If kind is "Cat":
            Define right-entry as cast build-state on (states, item 2 of tree's children, next).
            Return cast build-state on (states, item 1 of tree's children, right-entry).
        Done.
        If kind is "Or":
            Define left-entry as cast build-state on (states, item 1 of tree's children, next).
            Define right-entry as cast build-state on (states, item 2 of tree's children, next).
            Return cast emit-state on (states, 2, "", left-entry, right-entry).
        Done.
        If kind is "Opt":
            Define body-entry as cast build-state on (states, item 1 of tree's children, next).
            Return cast emit-state on (states, 2, "", body-entry, next).
        Done.
        // `*` and `+` differ only in where the loop is entered.
        Define branch as cast emit-state on (states, 2, "", 0, 0).
        Define body as cast build-state on (states, item 1 of tree's children, branch).
        The item branch of states becomes a record with (the kind 2, the ch "", the step body, the alt next).
        If kind is "Plus", return body.
        Return branch.
    Done.

    /// The automaton, or the fault in the C# parser's words at the declaration.
    Bind series of records like (the number kind, the text ch, the number step, the number alt) or failure
            to compiled-pattern, given (the text written, the number row, the number column):
        Define characters as a chase.
        Insert written into characters.
        Define reader as a new pattern-reader {
            the source characters, the size the number of characters, the at 1,
            the folding false, the dot-all false, the multiline false,
            the codes a map from text to number, the declared-row row, the declared-column column }.
        Define root as cast reader's read-alternation or pass the failure off.
        If cast reader's at-end is false and cast reader's peek-char is ")":
            Return a failure (cast reader's fault on ("this pattern closes a group that was never opened",
                "every ')' needs a '(' before it", "write '\\)' if you meant the character")).
        Done.
        Define states as a series of records like (the number kind, the text ch, the number step, the number alt).
        // Index 1 is reserved first and filled in last: the entry is state 1.
        Insert a record with (the kind 2, the ch "", the step 0, the alt 0) into states.
        Define accept as cast emit-state on (states, 3, "", 0, 0).
        Define entry-state as cast build-state on (states, root, accept).
        The item 1 of states becomes a record with (the kind 2, the ch "", the step entry-state, the alt entry-state).
        Return states.
    Done.
Done.
